								Sr. Member<br />
								<img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 495<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?action=profile;u=91"><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.myspace.com/flowside" title="Myspace" target="_blank"><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
							</div>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=154.msg1975#msg1975"><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=154.msg1975#msg1975">Re: Southern Rap Appreciation Thread</a></b>
									<div class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #1 on:</b> October 21, 2006, 12:33:09 am &#187;</div></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">I&#039;ve been hooked on Project Pat ever since I saw the video for Good Googly Moogly. He takes no shame in what he&#039;s doing and he believes in his music so much that he will take the listener consequence. There is a big amount of (listen) respek in that. UGK&#039;s Ridin&#039; Dirty is a favorite, simply because their Ridin&#039; Dirty is 3000% better than Chamillionaire&#039;s. One Day is on some truth shit and Diamonds &amp; Wood is a good song to vibe out to. I listen to this album on the bus frequently. 3 6 Mafia is known to bang out some pretty solid beats. Sure the lyrics are subpar, but sometimes you need some fun music. Scarface is just solid all around. C-Murder must be the most talented rapper in the history of rap simply for holding the (unofficial) record for most albums released while in prison. I think he even shot a video. That takes some serious cajones.</div>
						</td>
					</tr>
