							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;"><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=154.msg1977#msg1977">Quote from: eric. on October 21, 2006, 01:28:14 am</a></div><div class="quote">Wow. I hope your kidding? These dudes have no talent (that c-murder cover should be in the worst covers thread).. I know you have your own personal interests/opinions.. but i dont understand this. <br /><br />Project Pat&#039;s song &quot;Fuck A Bitch&quot;... CORNY ASS beat.. and for about 90 seconds it just says &quot;fuck a bitch, mothafuck a bitch..&quot;.... what kind of shit is that?!<br /><br />&nbsp;<img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Smileys/default/angry.gif" alt="Angry" border="0" /><br /></div><br />it&#039;s all a matter of preferences I guess.&nbsp; I bet if you asked most people who they would prefer listening to, Slug or say... Crunchy Black ( <img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Smileys/default/grin.gif" alt="Grin" border="0" />) they would say Crunchy in a second.&nbsp; Whether or not they prefer Crunchy for his hilariously bad lyrics or dislike Slug because he at times can come off a little pretentious is beyond the point... Saying you dislike the music is one thing, but to deny that anyone here has talent is if I may be so bold a little presumptuous on your behalf... Fiend is an accomplished ghostwriter and lyricist in his own right, Scarface is a legend hands down, Bun B is one of the dopest mc&#039;s out, Pimp C produced all those crazy UGK tracks that people still knock to this day... what else... well Project Pat is an acquired taste I must admit but from a musicality standpoint his voice is cool and his lyrics, while laced with filth and debauchery, make for a fine listen when the mood is right.&nbsp; Sometimes Eric when girls get you angry, it is ok to say &quot;Bitch, fuck you!&quot;&nbsp; As far as the beat is concerned, sometimes 3-6 doesnt come correct in my opinion, but to shift it back to a bridge of criticism towards who I would assume you like (Ant), sometimes his snares make my head want to pop.&nbsp; A matter of tastes is all I&#039;m saying.&nbsp; <br /><br />Liking or disliking is one thing, but to deny the talents of the aforementioned artist isn&#039;t fair&nbsp; <img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Smileys/default/grin.gif" alt="Grin" border="0" /></div>
