							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;"><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=154.msg2014#msg2014">Quote from: eric. on October 21, 2006, 02:31:36 pm</a></div><div class="quote">I wouldn&#039;t call myself uninformed.. i&#039;ve heard A LOT of southern rap.. and most of it sucked, bad.</div><br />You really have to listen to &quot;One Day.&quot; Bun B is what I like to call &quot;original talent.&quot; He is part of the group that defined what the southern sound is. UGK turned onto the sub 80bpm while everyone else in the hip hop world was still rocking 90+. I think what it might be is the fact that you&#039;re unable to relate to it, and that&#039;s cool, a lot of people don&#039;t listen to music that they just don&#039;t &quot;get.&quot; I see it as a slice of life type of art, where even though I can&#039;t relate to where he&#039;s coming from, I take it in like another part of our society.<br /><br />Besides, since when did every song have to be really deep and filled with punnery for it to be good? I find it hard to believe that you don&#039;t have a stash of party music somewhere that you rock out to when you need to unwind.</div>
